<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly residue down, distillates mixed.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly residue down, distillates mixed.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks fell by 926,000 barrels in the week ended January 15 to 10.074 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks also fell by 1.174 million barrels to 6.543 million barrels. Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Light distillate stocks rose by 75,000 barrels to 5.911 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha. -- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3084)</p>
